      "bio_html": "<p class=\"bio bio-lead\">He is a specialist in internal medicine, cardiology, and intensive care medicine. He is the author of more than 10 scientific articles and his research has been published in prestigious international scientific journals. He completed his medical doctorate at the University of Cologne in 2024. He holds a Master of Health Business Administration (MHBA). He has given presentations at many international scientific conferences. On many occasions, he represented the Federal Republic of Germany and spoke at international cardiology conferences held in Azerbaijan. He informed his colleagues about the latest scientific research and modern cardiac operations. He reviews manuscripts for the journal \"Clinical Research in Cardiology.\" He is a Fellow of the European Society of Cardiology (FESC).</p><p class=\"bio\">He began working as a resident physician in Bielefeld, Germany, in 2012. He is an Associate Professor at Saarland University. His 2025 publication also lists an affiliation with the Department of Internal Medicine III, Cardiology, Angiology, and Intensive Care Medicine at Saarland University Medical Center in Homburg, Germany.</p><p class=\"bio\">His research interests include atrial fibrillation, catheter ablation, pulsed field ablation, and long-term arrhythmia outcomes. He collaborates with colleagues at Azerbaijan Medical University on the “Cardiovascular Disease Burden in Azerbaijan” study.</p>",
