    "x.zeynalova@gmail.com": {
      "title": "Composer, musicologist, and researcher; Chair, BRIDGE OF SOUND, Germany; Founder and Artistic Director, BRIDGE OF SOUND orchestra; Founder, Curator, and Artistic Director, HARMONY OF SOUND International Music Festival",
      "bio_html": "<p class=\"bio bio-lead\">Khadija Zeynalova studied composition and musicology at Baku Music Academy from 1994 to 2000, completing her bachelor’s and master’s studies with distinction. She continued her composition studies at Hochschule für Musik Detmold in 2005–2006. From 2006 to 2012, she pursued doctoral studies at Paderborn University, where she defended her dissertation on Azerbaijani musical culture in the 20th century and its reception of Western music with distinction.</p><p class=\"bio\">Her teaching experience includes Hochschule für Musik Detmold and Azerbaijan State University of Culture and Arts, where she taught from 2000 to 2005.</p><p class=\"bio\">She was the first Azerbaijani composer and musicologist to receive a doctoral scholarship from the Friedrich-Ebert-Stiftung in Germany. She has also received scholarships from DAAD, the culture ministry of North Rhine-Westphalia, GVL, GEMA, and Musikfonds.</p><p class=\"bio\">She is the author of a doctoral dissertation on musicology and art studies, one scholarly book on composition published in Germany, 35 books published in Azerbaijan, Holland, Japan, England, and Germany, and 10 articles published in scholarly journals. She has presented her research at 20 international academic conferences and has created and served as artistic director of approximately 20 international projects, festivals, and concerts.</p><p class=\"bio\">In 2020, she received a Letter of Appreciation from Azerbaijan’s State Committee on Work with Diaspora for her contribution to communicating information about Azerbaijan internationally and her active involvement in diaspora development.</p><p class=\"bio\">In 2021, she was awarded the Republic of Azerbaijan’s “880th anniversary of Nizami” medal. That year, she also received a Certificate of Appreciation for participating as a composer in TURKSOY’s “Masterpieces of the Turkish World” project during the Year of Nizami and Yunus Emre.</p><p class=\"bio\">In 2022, she received the Republic of Azerbaijan’s “For Service in Diaspora Activity” medal at the 5th Congress of World Azerbaijanis in Shusha.</p><p class=\"bio\">In 2024, as the first Azerbaijani composer in Germany, she was awarded the nomination “Composer and Artist of the Year” by the German Ministry of Culture and Klosterlandschaft OWL.</p><p class=\"bio\">At the 1st Forum of Azerbaijani Culture Ambassadors in Antalya on November 3–5, 2025, she received an Honorary Decree recognizing her contribution as a composer to promoting Azerbaijani musical culture internationally.</p><p class=\"bio\">In 2026, she was awarded the “Progress” medal by decree of the President of the Republic of Azerbaijan, Ilham Aliyev, for her contributions to strengthening friendship between peoples and developing the Azerbaijani diaspora.</p>",
      "country": "Germany",
      "ixtilas": "Musician"
    },
    "mussa_98@hotmail.de": {
      "title": "Engineer and technology executive, Germany",
      "bio_html": "<p class=\"bio bio-lead\">Yashar Musayev is an engineer and technology executive specializing in green hydrogen, renewable energy, surface engineering, nanotechnology, and automotive technologies. His international experience combines research and development, industrial production, technology strategy, and collaboration with universities and research institutes.</p><p class=\"bio\">He studied Mechanical Engineering Technology at Azerbaijan Technical University from 1984 to 1991, graduating with distinction with a Dipl.-Ing. degree. He held a DAAD scholarship at Friedrich-Alexander-Universität Erlangen-Nürnberg (FAU) in 1997–1998 and completed his doctoral research there in 1998–2001, earning the Dr.-Ing. degree. He also participated in Schaeffler’s International Development Program for Top Managers in 2016–2020.</p><p class=\"bio\">In May 2020, he joined Siemens Energy AG in Erlangen/Munich as Head of Development for New Energy Business. His responsibilities included the development of green hydrogen, electrolysis, and renewable energy technologies, together with technology strategy and team leadership.</p><p class=\"bio\">From December 2005 to January 2020, he worked at Schaeffler AG in Herzogenaurach. He progressed from Project Leader for establishing the Coating Center to Team Lead and Expert, Director of the Coating Center, and Senior Vice President and Head of the Competency Center for Surface Technology, a position he held from September 2015 to January 2020. His responsibilities covered international research and production activities, coating technologies, supplier development, and partnerships with universities and research institutes.</p><p class=\"bio\">As a Schaeffler representative, he led the acquisition and integration of Naco Technologies in Riga in December 2015. Alongside his other responsibilities, he served as CEO of SIA Schaeffler Baltic from February 2016 to December 2018, directing research, development, and sales activities in the Baltic States.</p><p class=\"bio\">His earlier positions included Head of Research and Development at H-O-T in Nuremberg (2001–2005), Research Associate at FAU (2000–2001), Plant Manager at Autostern, a joint-venture partner of Daimler AG in Azerbaijan (1998–2000), and research and teaching roles at Azerbaijan Technical University (1991–1997).</p><p class=\"bio\">His work since 2005 includes more than 40 inventions and patents and 150 national and international publications and lectures.</p><p class=\"bio-section-title\">Awards and recognition:</p><div class=\"awards-block\"><ul class=\"awards-list\"><li><strong>Customer Supplier Award</strong> from a global Japanese automotive manufacturer (2017).</li><li><strong>Materialica Design + Technology Best-Award</strong> for Sensotect® thin-film sensors, Munich (2014, 2016).</li><li><strong>Customer Innovation Award</strong> for engine components from a global Japanese automotive manufacturer (2006).</li></ul></div><p class=\"bio\">He is a founding member of Nano in Germany e.V. and a member of the Association of German Engineers (VDI). He has served as Chairman of the Board of BalticNet-Plasmatech e.V. and Baku-Nürnberg e.V.</p><p class=\"bio-section-title\">Research and professional interests:</p><ul><li>Green hydrogen, electrolysis, renewable energy, and fuel-cell technologies.</li><li>Surface engineering, coating technologies, nanotechnology, and tribology.</li><li>Thin-film sensors, automotive technologies, and electric mobility.</li><li>Research and development management, technology strategy, and international scientific collaboration.</li></ul><p class=\"bio\">He speaks native Azerbaijani, fluent German, English, and Russian, and conversational Turkish.</p>",
      "country": "Germany",
      "ixtilas": "Engineering"
    },
