    "dinara_abasova@hotmail.com": {
      "title": "Associate Professor in Nuclear Chemistry; nuclear scientist and consultant, Vienna, Austria",
      "bio_html": "<p class=\"bio bio-lead\">Dinara Abbasova is a nuclear scientist and consultant with more than 23 years of international experience in nuclear and radiation chemistry, radioactive waste management, knowledge management, and capacity building. Her work combines scientific research with project management, international collaboration, professional training, and the development of educational materials.</p><p class=\"bio\">She studied chemistry at Baku State University, completing her bachelor’s studies in 1998–2002 and master’s studies in 2002–2004. She earned a PhD in Radiation Chemistry at the Institute of Radiation Problems of the Azerbaijan National Academy of Sciences in 2012 and obtained the academic title of Associate Professor in 2016. In 2022–2024, she completed an Executive MBA in Strategic Project Management at the Vienna University of Economics and Business.</p><p class=\"bio\">She worked as a consultant at the International Atomic Energy Agency (IAEA) in 2017–2019 and 2023–2025. Her responsibilities included scientific support for the Convention on Nuclear Safety, the development of e-learning and training materials, and contributions to IAEA publications. From 2020 to 2023, she worked as a scientist in knowledge management at Helmholtz-Zentrum Dresden-Rossendorf (HZDR), contributing to radioactive waste management under EURAD and serving as a knowledge management expert in the PIANOFORTE Partnership.</p><p class=\"bio\">Earlier, she was a Visiting Professor at the Institute of Geology of the Polish Academy of Sciences (2012–2015) and a consultant at Delta Unlimited (2015–2017). At the Institute of Radiation Problems (2004–2012), her roles included Head of the National INIS Center, Scientific Secretary, Chromatography Expert, and Quality Manager. She began her career as a Chromatography Expert and Quality Manager at Azlab Oil Company (2002–2004).</p><p class=\"bio\">Her international activities include work as an IAEA knowledge management expert, a European Commission expert in radiation chemistry, and an OECD/NEA IDKM liaison to an ISO working group on knowledge management in radioactive waste management. She is a member of Women in Nuclear (WiN Global). She was a <strong>Simons Associate (2015–2020)</strong> at the Abdus Salam International Centre for Theoretical Physics (ICTP).</p><p class=\"bio\">Her honors include recognition for achievement in science from Azerbaijan’s Ministry of Youth and Sports (2010), an IAEA fellowship (2010), recognition as a Young Nuclear Professional Woman of Azerbaijan (2012), appreciation from the UAE Permanent Mission to the IAEA (2019), and an IAEA certificate recognizing voluntary support (2024).</p><p class=\"bio\"><strong>Research and professional interests:</strong></p><ul><li>Nuclear and radiation chemistry, radiation protection, and radioactive waste management.</li><li>Isotope and radiocarbon analysis, chromatography, and alpha and gamma spectrometry.</li><li>Environmental monitoring, quality assurance, and the application of international standards.</li><li>Nuclear knowledge preservation and transfer, professional training, and e-learning.</li></ul><p class=\"bio\">She speaks Azerbaijani and Russian as native languages, is fluent in English and Polish, and has intermediate proficiency in German and Italian.</p>",
      "country": "Austria",
      "ixtilas": "Chemistry"
    },
    "kamal.akbarov@gmail.com": {
