f the CCP4 executive committee – this committee brings together leading international researchers in the field of computational structural biology.</li></ul></div><p class=\"bio-section-title\">Publications and scientific contributions:</p><p class=\"bio\">He is the author of more than 120 high-impact scientific articles, including in prestigious journals such as Nature, Science, PNAS and Acta Crystallographica.</p><p class=\"bio\">He was a leading researcher in the development of innovative software (REFMAC5, SERVALCAT, EMDA, BALBES, AceDRG) for the analysis and modeling of molecular structures.</p><p class=\"bio\">He regularly participates in international symposia and conferences and organizes scientific seminars in different countries (Great Britain, Japan, China, USA, Brazil, India, etc.).</p>",
