 works. His works have been translated into Estonian, Georgian, Russian, Latvian, German, English and most Turkish languages.</p><p class=\"bio\">More than 40 socio-political, historical and scientific-cultural articles,</p><p class=\"bio\">6 books and 1 monograph,</p><p class=\"bio\">He is the author of 4 scientific articles published in 2 scientific journals.</p><p class=\"bio\">He is a speaker and participant of more than 20 international symposia and conferences.</p><p class=\"bio\">Professional and academic activities</p><p class=\"bio\">Finno-Ugric and Turkic Peoples Research Center - chairman</p><p class=\"bio\">University of Tartu (Estonia) - Director of the Turkish Language Center</p><p class=\"bio\">World Congress of Azerbaijanis - Member of the Management Board, Deputy Chairman</p><p class=\"bio\">Estonian-Azerbaijani Society - chairman</p><p class=\"bio\">World Union of Azerbaijani Scientists - member of the Organization Committee</p><p class=\"bio\">Azerbaijan Union of Writers - member</p><p class=\"bio\">Estonian Society of Academic Orientalists - member</p><p class=\"bio\">Turkish Literature Foundation - honorary member</p><p class=\"bio\">Diplomatic and translation activities</p><p class=\"bio\">Khagani Gayibli participated as a translator in high-level official meetings in Estonia and Turkey. He was a special interpreter during the official visits of the presidents, parliament speakers and ministers of Azerbaijan, Turkey and Estonia.</p>",
